<title>USA: Household sees earnings boost from deal.</title>
<headline>Household sees earnings boost from deal.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Household International Inc said Monday it expects its $1.1 billion purchase of the consumer finance business of Transamerica Corp will be slightly accretive to 1997 earnings.</p>
<p>It also expects the deal to add $0.15 to $0.20 a share to 1998 earnings.</p>
<p>&quot;That's the guidance we're giving,&quot; a Household spokesman said.</p>
<p>Earlier, Household said the acquisition will help it increase its network of consumer finance offices under the HFC brand.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
